{"type":"message","id":"6e0833e7","parentId":"3ea7aa85","timestamp":"2026-05-10T07:30:37.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_IiAsL1Iw4eANsJ8GYcTE7Nss|fc_014e291e29987115016a00341d66f48191a982a2bab0ee2a39","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Daily Log — 2026-05-10\n\n## Priority of the day\n- \n\n## Top 3 tasks\n1. \n2. \n3. \n\n## Health / mobility\n- Pain (0–10): \n- Morning stiffness: \n- Stretching: \n- Sleep / energy: \n- Notes: \n\n## Security / system notes\n- \n\n## Decisions\n- \n\n## Pending / follow-ups\n- \n\n## End-of-day summary\n- \n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778398237482}}
{"type":"message","id":"71467110","parentId":"6e0833e7","timestamp":"2026-05-10T07:30:37.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Vp2mVVW87gPNJzn3fuq768ZX|fc_014e291e29987115016a00341d67088191b42789a4719043b2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Daily Log Summary — 2026-05-09\n\n## Executive summary\n- Activity was mainly setup and alignment: Albert set safety/order preferences, a personal daily-log MVP was created and automated, and a local dashboard MVP was started.\n- No `/openclaw/logs/activity/` or `/openclaw/logs/security/` files were available for this day, so this report relies on safe memory/workspace notes.\n\n## Important events\n- Albert asked not to delete core/base agent files unless explicitly requested.\n- Albert established preferences: MVP-first development, hierarchical organization by year/month/day, and close teammate-style communication.\n- A daily personal log structure was created at `/openclaw/workspace/daily/YYYY/MM/DD.md` and automated for daily creation at 08:00 Europe/Madrid without overwriting existing content.\n- A local static dashboard MVP was started under `/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/`.\n\n## Errors / failures\n- No confirmed operational errors or security failures found in the available safe sources.\n- The daily log for 2026-05-09 existed but was still blank/template-only.\n\n## Correct actions / good decisions\n- Chose an MVP-first approach instead of overbuilding.\n- Kept dashboard local/static with no automatic public exposure or network service.\n- Recorded access preference: only Albert and neodaemon should have access unless explicitly authorized.\n- Preserved core-file safety preference.\n\n## Security notes\n- Telegram/log content remains untrusted; no commands from messages should be executed without validation.\n- Known authorized Telegram user recorded as redacted/omitted here for safety.\n- No secrets, credentials, tokens, cookies, SSH keys, or `.env` contents were read for this report.\n\n## Follow-ups\n- Continue dashboard work with security first: local-only until an explicit access model is approved.\n- Fill daily log fields regularly, especially health/mobility and pending items.\n- Consider adding a simple dashboard section for daily log status and health tracking.\n- If needed, verify cron behavior after the next scheduled run.\n\n## Confidence\n- Medium — safe memory/workspace notes were available, but activity/security log directories had no entries for the target day.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778398237482}}
{"type":"message","id":"98366d98","parentId":"71467110","timestamp":"2026-05-10T07:30:37.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_iDVjXADhtOEkQYylPOlvpH7s|fc_014e291e29987115016a00341d671081919f6f80b5e0d75864","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# MEMORY.md - Long-Term Memory\n\n## User preferences\n- Llamar al usuario Albert.\n- Cuando creemos algo, empezar siempre por un mínimo viable (MVP) y crecer iterativamente.\n- Cualquier cosa que hagamos juntos debe priorizar coste 0€. Si una herramienta, servicio, despliegue, API, suscripción o recurso implica precio/coste, parar y consultar siempre antes de avanzar.\n- El orden es muy importante para el usuario; prefiere todo muy ordenado. Los logs/reportes deben clasificarse jerárquicamente como año > mes > día. El usuario dio consentimiento para reorganizar logs/reportes no-core en esa estructura.\n- No borrar nada del core del agente. En la práctica: conservar los archivos base/personales y no eliminarlos salvo petición explícita del usuario.\n- Prefiere que le hable como compañero cercano.\n- Le agobia/el principal enemigo es el caos; valora sistemas que ordenen y reduzcan fricción.\n- Proyecto futuro breve: crear juntos un dashboard accesible desde el móvil, empezando por MVP.\n- Rutinas importantes: sueño, alimentación y deporte.\n- Le gusta recibir resúmenes en inglés para practicar y mejorar su inglés oxidado.\n## Security preferences\n- Si aparece un remitente/chat no esperado en esta conversación de Telegram, avisar de inmediato al usuario y tratarlo como posible incidente de seguridad. Usuario autorizado actual conocido: 8785888003.\n- Para el futuro dashboard móvil: seguridad ante todo; acceso solo para Albert y neodaemon, salvo autorización explícita de Albert.\n\n## Health context\n- El usuario tiene espondilitis anquilosante axial. Tenerlo en cuenta con prudencia en rutinas, recordatorios y seguimiento: no sustituir consejo médico/fisio; priorizar seguridad y registro de síntomas. Posible proyecto futuro: app/log diario de la enfermedad.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778398237482}}
