{"type":"message","id":"7b23f816","parentId":"de6f8d8f","timestamp":"2026-05-10T08:27:33.376Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning technical updates**\n\nI think I need to dig deeper into daily reports; maybe a max depth of 5? I might also check git status, but I wonder if that’s really necessary. The plan shouldn’t require any paid services, so I need to clarify if “tokens per task” need a data source. I should review cron and logs, focusing on session status for the current state. Before adjusting anything, I’ll analyze the architecture based on previous readings. Importantly, I won’t apply any modifications until I have a solid plan in place.\n\n**Proposing project phases**\n\nI’m thinking about breaking things down into phases for this project. For the MVP at zero cost, I’ll create a data ledger at /openclaw/workspace/metrics/token-efficiency/YYYY/MM/DD.jsonl. After meaningful tasks, I’ll append records with timestamps, channels, task details, status, useful scores, and token metrics. \n\nI could improve it with daily scans of session histories and cron runs to classify tasks. I should also add a static dashboard display for efficiency metrics. Lastly, I need some heuristic rules for repetitive tasks and identify any anomalies based on set thresholds.\n\n**Identifying potential risks**\n\nI need to consider some potential risks in my plans. Task detection could be subjective, and token counts are at a session level rather than per task. Snapshots might misattribute tokens if multiple tasks overlap. Privacy issues from scanning transcripts and automation could also inflate token consumption; plus, a static dashboard won’t update live without a script. Channel classification might not be comprehensive. I'll need to define what “real value” means and be wary of false positives. \n\nFor now, I plan to use only local files to keep costs at zero and ensure security with no network dependencies. I’ll seek approval for these options, as the user requested it, while also noting the constraints of current data sources.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_014e291e29987115016a004158c76481918ce78dea358db492\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAEFnwlBypUhQhWAXSFiI4ge-8IcTnGWxvjkra1DXVmJ3MymNeFws4Ntt_OLbWWuTVlSdObo9f75WaMVnmTCzb17U3y7HxiWg6ddn2AfvWF77uzuULqlAjXSt13lhcqeZjKSY5frgImcsij0JVxkiRXRzMK5mJd_6irkbMhwNJPwhgdnRdzfFeaeSCaNVE2I7yesSKXselLp0LCSNilecerVWmW3Oup1AJqBZWRwKrH6_6F8erzbkGZZqLSNW1ADcwnoTDlR8-KYROwDdN5OZcL7WeCMTTqeZwGctOECKo7Vz3VytZDfu3mr_76gsCGMoVu0WA_1glFPOk4qzqo2tyB51yo09daaV-4SAoMqlJQZ4jJY9Y1qD3APHIGX76MPzjP_lIihKHEKUUhK1Zk6fb5HrCrpo34aTfxwIElo7penCiVtXEEu5YDURgbeImtW-TTcxk-JpDjQps0gpj2fIRRcZ8x7D25U9SD5gl_-df6yN60g3MxYLgMjkt3ulRX-w5AssleJixKzuNhCwh02MZnSc9YX2sjaRiD6UEyY1s28ylpGmozSoNAUY41VYLG9RwEWihbGuNTvOM2BvEu8YjPMD9CZXb6oC0BURlgpot8hny-uIin_4f9EPBsrAw06kxOP0WKnRSMK2F-n-JiotUJFT8a3QbqF0sWeUwbr2Adc9I_JKoWTfg5H8kaW0crI_9_mOt83W25fFiCbzW4svgQzQRnq1k72On95WEFu21r5_pyRnUkgjzUNt1J4atoVjSz-F5eeX8exYavU76EVb5xtgfokAQEhvUFwI-cqSzmuPpNPCFdtjYgJPUKyT5VjYTn4HtopFtxs0f-e5WVh-0bAXmiZReEzitwNoURmoUCrGsZ9JnVQYcpXuHkC52Srvwk-Wft-bEY_zM4J8BIXHQPSxvlsGyiWC5ho2hOhAX6TMz1ZazRj37TwR8hQVUxSVgh8wnQbWdYIYxXv1DGpltsIsJGOwyR0Zm0S2byQcmv8ccWLb_pvTpmtLi-oGvt77zm-20d-OnXhgae_GqgubEk3v_3dn1kDTNRwLzrS-rgt-LQ2iXUvoATk_tsr7c3BUVaZqE3O9b8hVsMS0iUFlHMofi_BU0dJEJUbNj6kgzcf9ew5pYcZJ-IOcBVwRBCHNASCp1x0Y5vy-KKMavhr3X76CIAjkMKQnoXLhzWZr_-4JSpi--hwovQQaxMmaQMo4HUP3vpHgUYNC5xNvEpiRcM3lWhe49Zn-srZWg_HtS8O40Zqd2JHyV5vx-SG3joUyIzAoSCibLC_hdtrZlNoABPR3_Md05vyb3-0k0iH4Tov5wDNY5nFqiOAkDYYXTOC3w3S0ylaSnJWkMlMHceoQ71K5N7Y4JpDwAx_zGd0XkyCHS_sUCYNOi5yw2RQV79wymVdtAFcKe8nPZ0PEXxnYVZaXKgKwuF3wpMzgb2KyJYdxowwwsWNV0J73dQYeukMmOVhp86XWSJvFB7KH5IRBF-F7VZs0xlYUqIG3tsZ7oH4ZQz9NKLc1XhuSWFssksT0S0QlQaLYwW79mnntRH8p3TwiDzm7xw4jWVHdC5SNxuyUImLDlspWzptoVF2m9yLf3zz6DO8786AFg7KKiiIHahFXatxl-Xmpqit2_wZvUlURCKD8IT1MLAR5zfMHKz5YKjKCV4V_9DlpC8h4EMpB7dbY9jZQwPY9lzAucZbai3Oqe-J2es3HMR6De9lTq1d2sAFu9U18avzLMArg-G359pymk1MV8vQfR