{"type":"message","id":"9e6ed51a","parentId":"b4ed3f00","timestamp":"2026-05-10T08:30:29.362Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_afG5LMHY3iWkq8epVlHEQr5r|fc_014e291e29987115016a0042251f688191be5dc45f9f69a849","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Dashboard MVP\n\nLocal, static, read-only dashboard concept for Albert and neodaemon.\n\nSecurity principles:\n- Local files only for now.\n- No public exposure.\n- No network service started automatically.\n- No credentials or secrets stored here.\n- MVP first, iterate slowly.\n\nInitial blocks:\n1. Today\n2. Health / mobility\n3. Habits\n4. Pending / chaos inbox\n5. LLM token usage snapshot\n6. Token efficiency: “tokens per useful task”\n\nToken efficiency MVP:\n- Source: `/openclaw/workspace/metrics/token_efficiency/YYYY/MM/DD.jsonl`\n- Current values are estimated from `session_status` snapshots, not exact per-task accounting.\n- Channels are grouped as Telegram, TUI, automations, subagents, or unknown.\n- Visual bars are static CSS, with no external libraries or network calls.\n\nOpen `index.html` locally when explicitly approved/needed.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778401829360}}
