{"type":"message","id":"498e4d1c","parentId":"1295e771","timestamp":"2026-05-10T12:19:06.249Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Es el mismo diagnóstico, Albert: **Firefox es Snap**, así que `file://` puede fallar por permisos/mount namespace.\n\nUsa esta vía, que debería evitar el problema:\n\n```bash\ncd \"$(dirname \"$(realpath ./openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html)\")\"\npython3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1\n```\n\nLuego abre en Firefox:\n\n```text\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8765/\n```\n\nSi quieres hacerlo en una sola línea:\n\n```bash\ncd \"$(dirname \"$(realpath ./openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html)\")\" && python3 -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1\n```\n\nPara parar: `Ctrl+C`.\n\nNo abre internet ni cuesta nada: queda solo local en tu Ubuntu.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_014e291e29987115016a0077b6835c81918d93238d6ddb4ebd\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":695,"output":179,"cacheRead":42496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":43370,"cost":{"input":0.0034750000000000002,"output":0.00537,"cacheRead":0.021248,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.030093}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778415540310,"responseId":"resp_014e291e29987115016a0077b4f05c8191ba3c5009e3198353"}}
