{"type":"custom_message","customType":"openclaw.runtime-context","content":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:8785888003\",\n  \"message_id\": \"325\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"sender\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sun 2026-05-10 15:16 GMT+2\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw Bunker (8785888003)\",\n  \"id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"name\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\"\n}\n```","display":false,"details":{"source":"openclaw-runtime-context"},"id":"661f6b86","parentId":"a473a745","timestamp":"2026-05-10T13:16:25.128Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"11428a64","parentId":"661f6b86","timestamp":"2026-05-10T13:16:31.785Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sí, Albert. **Puede y debe ir con contraseña.**\n\nOpciones habituales en hosting web:\n\n**1. Protección de directorio con contraseña**\n- La más simple.\n- Suele estar en el panel del hosting como:\n  - “Directorios protegidos”\n  - “Password protected directories”\n  - “Privacidad de directorios”\n- Protege una carpeta tipo:\n  ```text\n  /dashboard\n  ```\n- Al entrar a:\n  ```text\n  dashboard.tudominio.com\n  ```\n  pide usuario y contraseña.\n\n**2. Archivo `.htaccess` + `.htpasswd`**\n- Muy común si el hosting usa Apache.\n- También es simple, pero más técnico.\n- Ventaja: no necesita programar nada.\n\n**3. Login dentro del propio dashboard**\n- Más bonito, pero más complejo.\n- No lo recomiendo para el MVP.\n\nMi recomendación: **opción 1**, desde el panel del hosting.  \nEs lo más simple, 0€ normalmente, y suficiente para un dashboard estático de solo lectura.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_014e291e29987115016a00852bbe008191a8f52df6d67ed7ac\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":2380,"output":220,"cacheRead":58368,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":60968,"cost":{"input":0.0119,"output":0.0066,"cacheRead":0.029183999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.047684000000000004}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778418985128,"responseId":"resp_014e291e29987115016a008529e3d48191822a8163dcef1e57"}}
{"type":"message","id":"b07281ae","parentId":"11428a64","timestamp":"2026-05-10T13:17:58.776Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Me parece bien todo lo que indicas, gracias. Neodaemon puedes crear una alerta si llegamos al 95% de consumo de tokens diarios?"}],"timestamp":1778419078774}}
{"type":"custom_message","customType":"openclaw.runtime-context","content":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:8785888003\",\n  \"message_id\": \"327\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"sender\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sun 2026-05-10 15:17 GMT+2\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw Bunker (8785888003)\",\n  \"id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"name\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\"\n}\n```","display":false,"details":{"source":"openclaw-runtime-context"},"id":"6b006dea","parentId":"b07281ae","timestamp":"2026-05-10T13:17:58.778Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"819d6df7","parentId":"6b006dea","timestamp":"2026-05-10T13:18:18.118Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering alert creation**\n\nI need to find a solution for creating an alert. Maybe I can use a cron job to schedule periodic checks around session status, specifically for usage left. An alert at 95% consumption would mean only 5% is left daily. Could I create a recurring isolated agentTurn to check the session status? I might use Telegram for notifications, which could alert every 30 minutes. However, I want to monitor usage accurately without overloading. It seems I need to be mindful of token consumption too.\n\n**Clarifying alert conditions**\n\nI need to figure out how to set up an alert that only triggers when a specific threshold is reached. If an isolated run can determine a NO_REPLY response, I wonder how delivery announcements work if they send summaries anyway. Using the systemEvent main might make sense for generating a heartbeat, so I can inject reminders to check without conditions. I’ll consider crons to check the session status and ensure alerts are set up properly without automatically triggering unless the threshold is met. I should seek out the sessionKey to assist with this too.\n\n**Deciding on alerts and responses**\n\nIt looks like I might not need an alert after all. I could try setting a delivery announcement while hoping that NO_REPLY is suppressed, but that isn’t guaranteed. An alternative would be to schedule a systemEvent in the main every hour as a reminder to check tokens and alert the user if necessary. This should produce NO_REPLY if no response is needed. I’ll also consider using a cron job with agentTurn to manage announcements for thresholds properly.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_014e291e29987115016a00858b9704819192b262e15441b545\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAIWXqIoT_KE1M97UOEVzIwAeJYt2YFw6-gz2WBiljADBAWp1hcpuiKYATx3YI98dxhnQua