ys, and I can suggest using a cron job for automation. Maybe a specific time like 10:00 could work? I just need to ensure we have all decisions in place to move forward effectively.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Scheduling audits every 15 days**\\n\\nI’m considering a way to schedule recurring audits every 15 days. I think it would be best to set the first one for May 25, 2026, at 10:00 AM in Europe/Madrid, providing a clear anchor point. I could also check with the user if they prefer a specific day or time since I want to make sure they’re happy with the arrangement. I should mention how audit tasks read without making changes, since tokens are a concern for the user. We need to balance efficiency and cost here.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Creating a protocol for scheduling**\\n\\nI’m thinking that since this is an automation task, it should run within the hours of 08:00 to 21:00. It might be wise to draft a protocol document first and wait for approval before scheduling anything. The user asked for my thoughts and how we can move forward, rather than just creating it. Perhaps I should suggest a plan and say something like, \\\"If you’re okay with it, I’ll schedule it for 10:00.\\\" I need to ensure the timing is clear before proceeding.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_W5EAAZD6Lq5ncKA9spaTpAt1|fc_014e291e29987115016a00def4821c8191996522043feb9132","name":"memory_search","arguments":{"query":"auditorías cada 15 días core general MEMORY.md regla memoria orden rigor seguridad automatizaciones noche","maxResults":5,"corpus":"memory"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":40496,"output":564,"cacheRead":65024,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":106084,"cost":{"input":0.20248000000000002,"output":0.01692,"cacheRead":0.032512,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.251912}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778441946059,"responseId":"resp_014e291e29987115016a00dedbbe208191991cf845d1e2f440"}}
{"type":"message","id":"078a2b6e","parentId":"ea605a62","timestamp":"2026-05-10T19:39:33.951Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_W5EAAZD6Lq5ncKA9spaTpAt1|fc_014e291e29987115016a00def4821c8191996522043feb9132","toolName":"memory_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"MEMORY.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1,\n      \"endLine\": 15,\n      \"score\": 0.5195483773946762,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.7422119677066803,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"# MEMORY.md - Long-Term Memory\\n\\n## User preferences\\n- Llamar al usuario Albert.\\n- Cuando creemos algo, empezar siempre por un mínimo viable (MVP) y crecer iterativamente.\\n- Cualquier cosa que hagamos juntos debe priorizar coste 0€. Si una herramienta, servicio, despliegue, API, suscripción o recurso implica precio/coste, parar y consultar siempre antes de avanzar.\\n- El orden es muy importante para el usuario; prefiere todo muy ordenado. Los logs/reportes deben clasificarse jerárquicamente como año > mes > día. El usuario dio consentimiento para reorganizar logs/reportes no-core en esa estructura.\\n- No borrar nada del core del agente. En la práctica: conservar los archivos base/personales y n\\n\\nSource: MEMORY.md#L1-L15\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"MEMORY.md#L1-L15\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026/05/10.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 9,\n      \"endLine\": 13,\n      \"score\": 0.5167734056711196,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.7382477223873138,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- Albert confirmó como principio rector: “Orden, rigor y seguridad”. La regla queda fijada: primero ordenar, luego medir, después automatizar solo lo seguro.\\n- Albert indicó que ha creado un correo propio e individual de Gmail para neodaemon. No guardar credenciales en memoria ni en chats; usarlo solo tras definir protocolo seguro de acceso/uso.\\n- Albert aprobó auditar tools/plugins tras revisar el core. Se hizo auditoría solo lectura y se guardó en `/personal/albert/auditoria-tools-plugins-2026-05-10.md`: 92 plugins descubiertos, 67 loaded, 25 disabled, plugin doctor limpio, 7 skills elegibles, 3 cron activos, y advertencias de seguridad sobre allowlist de grupos Telegram, trusted proxies s\\n\\nSource: memory/2026/05/10.md#L9-L13\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026/05/10.md#L9-L13\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026/05/10.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 6,\n      \"endLine\": 10,\n      \"score\": 0.4939681231975555,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.7056687474250793,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- Albert envió un PDF con un protocolo más estricto previo a dar acceso a Internet a OpenClaw. Se fusionó en `/personal/albert/protocolo-acceso-internet.md`: fase 0 con requisitos previos, política de solo lectura inicial, sandboxing, observabilidad obligatoria, human-in-the-loop, allowlist, rate limiting, modo observación 7–14 días y sistema de emergencia.\\n- Albert indicó que tiene hosting web, dominio propio y quiere acceder al dashboard desde fuera de casa. Recomendación pendiente: empezar con dashboard estático solo lectura protegido, sin exponer OpenClaw ni herramientas internas.\\n- Se creó una alerta cron cada 30 minutos para revisar el consumo diario de tokens de la sesión principal de\\n\\nSource: memory/2026/05/10.md#L6-L10\",\n      \"source\": \"memory\",\n      \"citation\": \"memory/2026/05/10.md#L6-L10\",\n      \"corpus\": \"memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"memory/2026-05-09.md\",\n      \"startLine\": 1,\n      \"endLine\": 8,\n      \"score\": 0.4878393948078155,\n      \"vectorScore\": 0.6969134211540222,\n      \"textScore\": 0,\n      \"snippet\": \"- El usuario indicó: \\\"No borres nada de tu core\\\". Interpretación operativa: no eliminar archivos base/personales del agente (AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, USER.md, TOOLS.md, HEARTBE